⛬  OpenAlgo Python SDK Alignment
   •  The openalgo SDK wraps REST and websocket endpoints
      (placeorder, basketorder, data/position/funds queries,
      live LTP/quote/depth streams) via api(api_key, host, 
      ws_url) and expects payload keys like price_type,
      product, strategy, plus direct helpers for smart,
      basket, split orders, and analyzer toggles.
   •  Our current OpenAlgoClient manually reimplements a
      limited subset of REST calls (place_order, get_quotes,
      get_positions, etc.), omits websocket support and
      higher-level helpers, and slightly diverges from
      expected payload names (order_type vs price_type,
      missing strategy), which could break compatibility.
   •  To stay on track, either adopt the official
      openalgo.api client (leveraging its richer
      functionality and upstream updates) or adjust our
      wrapper to mirror the SDK’s request schemas, additional        
       endpoints, and websocket interfaces while validating
      the correct auth headers (Authorization vs SDK’s
      default behavior).

